# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a strand that reaches DEAD state is returned to the strand pool;
#         a subsequent allocation reuses the same slot without new allocation.
#
# defer-to: M5 or v1.x
#
# Reason: strand pooling (recycle-after-DEAD) is not implemented at M3.
# The M3 strand C API (T20) allocates strands fresh from the VM allocator
# and frees them on destroy; no free-list or pool exists yet.  Pool recycling
# is a memory-optimisation deferred to M5 (stdlib) or v1.x (performance pass).
# This fixture also requires host-driver infrastructure (T39) to observe
# pool internals from a chk fixture.
#
# When the strand pool lands, implement this fixture by:
#   ## host: run strand A to completion; record its allocation address
#   ## host: allocate strand B; assert it reuses strand A's slot
